WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
Why do we use letters in maths?

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.100
A letter stands for a number we don't know yet.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.490
n + 3 = 10

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.780
The letter is a box waiting to be filled.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:19.968
Here, n = 7.
